Description: Choose a desktop OpenGL config for a stereo window on an EGL that offers two views
 Qt takes an OpenGL ES config on NVIDIA's EGL (desktop OpenGL there is "for
 development purposes"). A stereo window needs desktop OpenGL: its two views are
 the left and right back buffers, and the decorations context of a window under
 Qt's own frame (stereo3d-wayland-egl-eye-slots) is a desktop OpenGL context made
 from the window's config. On NVIDIA's EGL with the gl-stereo layer's two views
 (EGL_EXT_multiview_window) the config had no EGL_OPENGL_BIT, the decorations
 context could not be created ("Failed to create the decorations EGLContext") and
 the window stayed black wherever the compositor offers no server-side frame.
 .
 q_desktopGLAllowed() keeps the exception for NVIDIA's EGL and lifts it for a
 stereo format on a display that lists EGL_EXT_multiview_window, in the config
 chooser and in the format Qt reads back from the config. NVIDIA's own EGL does
 not list the extension, so a program without the layer, and every non-stereo
 format, keep OpenGL ES as before.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
---
diff --git a/src/gui/opengl/platform/egl/qeglconvenience.cpp b/src/gui/opengl/platform/egl/qeglconvenience.cpp
index fbcd29e9..eb2516f3 100644
--- a/src/gui/opengl/platform/egl/qeglconvenience.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/opengl/platform/egl/qeglconvenience.cpp
@@ -202,6 +202,20 @@ QEglConfigChooser::~QEglConfigChooser()
 {
 }
 
+#ifndef QT_NO_OPENGL
+// NVIDIA EGL only provides desktop GL for development purposes, and recommends against using it.
+// A stereo format is the exception where the display offers two views of a window surface
+// (EGL_EXT_multiview_window, as the gl-stereo layer gives over NVIDIA's EGL): those views are
+// the left and right back buffers of desktop OpenGL, and the platform's decorations context
+// for such a window is a desktop OpenGL context that needs a config of that API.
+static bool q_desktopGLAllowed(EGLDisplay display, const QSurfaceFormat &format)
+{
+    const char *vendor = eglQueryString(display, EGL_VENDOR);
+    return !vendor || !strstr(vendor, "NVIDIA")
+            || (format.stereo() && q_hasEglExtension(display, "EGL_EXT_multiview_window"));
+}
+#endif // QT_NO_OPENGL
+
 EGLConfig QEglConfigChooser::chooseConfig()
 {
     QList<EGLint> configureAttributes = q_createConfigAttributesFromFormat(m_format);
@@ -217,9 +231,7 @@ EGLConfig QEglConfigChooser::chooseConfig()
 #ifdef EGL_VERSION_1_4
     case QSurfaceFormat::DefaultRenderableType: {
 #ifndef QT_NO_OPENGL
-        // NVIDIA EGL only provides desktop GL for development purposes, and recommends against using it.
-        const char *vendor = eglQueryString(display(), EGL_VENDOR);
-        if (QOpenGLContext::openGLModuleType() == QOpenGLContext::LibGL && (!vendor || !strstr(vendor, "NVIDIA")))
+        if (QOpenGLContext::openGLModuleType() == QOpenGLContext::LibGL && q_desktopGLAllowed(display(), m_format))
             configureAttributes.append(EGL_OPENGL_BIT);
         else
 #endif // QT_NO_OPENGL
@@ -375,7 +387,7 @@ QSurfaceFormat q_glFormatFromConfig(EGLDisplay display, const EGLConfig config,
     else if (referenceFormat.renderableType() == QSurfaceFormat::DefaultRenderableType
 #ifndef QT_NO_OPENGL
              && QOpenGLContext::openGLModuleType() == QOpenGLContext::LibGL
-             && !strstr(eglQueryString(display, EGL_VENDOR), "NVIDIA")
+             && q_desktopGLAllowed(display, referenceFormat)
 #endif
              && (renderableType & EGL_OPENGL_BIT))
         format.setRenderableType(QSurfaceFormat::OpenGL);
